    "body": "> Currently there are no protections against collisions from [#dfn-generate-a-random-uuid](https://w3c.github.io/webcrypto/#dfn-generate-a-random-uuid), but allowing it to be passed could make us more exposed here, at least if it's implemented verbatim in an engine. Is there a way for us to protect against that?\r\n\r\nIn w3c/webdriver-bidi#1180 the only caller that passes `navigationId` is WebDriver BiDi's \"await a navigation\", which generates a new random UUID each time it calls navigate. It cannot be supplied by the command parameters. So as far as I can tell the collision risks are the same as with the IDs that navigate generates itself.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
