    "updated_at": "2026-11-18T07:55:19Z",
    "body": "Yeah, this is a very hypothetical where someone can control how `#navigate` is called and maliciously do things with known UUIDs. An alternative would to optionally pass a state struct where the id is a member, then `#navigate` could store what it generates and WebDriver BiDi's \"await a navigation\" could pass such a state and read out what `#navigate` generates.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
