    "created_at": "2026-11-23T16:10:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T16:10:41Z",
    "body": "Question Q1 is open. No other design issues found.\n\n> I guess I'd like an editor weigh in perhaps.\n\nQ1: a caller-supplied `navigationId` can equal the ID of a navigation that's still in progress ([farre](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13078#issuecomment-6951632297)). If navigable N's ongoing navigation is X and someone calls navigate(N, B) with `navigationId` X, \"set the ongoing navigation\" returns early, so X isn't aborted and both navigations can commit. WebDriver BiDi generates a fresh UUID per call, so it can't hit this today. Also, \"a UUID string generated during navigation\" no longer fits a caller-supplied ID. Open, no fix yet.\n\n- a. Keep as is: the only caller generates a fresh ID each time, and it's the same shape as the `navigationId` parameter navigate had from 0969d8d until 0a97a81.\n- b. Assert in navigate that `navigationId` isn't another navigation's ID, and update the definition ([option b](https://github.com/zcorpan/html/commit/c684fdf2c152a2d58ff0fd60e5e23fb6f0b4d8d6)): small, and no BiDi change, but nothing enforces it beyond the assert.\n- c. navigate always generates the ID and passes it to an optional `onNavigationId` algorithm ([option c](https://github.com/zcorpan/html/commit/a25d6efc2f614d4c09349c83431f10a33b0903a5); [farre's suggestion](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/13078#issuecomment-6972568415), as a callback instead of a struct): navigate stays responsible for uniqueness, but w3c/webdriver-bidi#1180 needs reworking. Also, the callback doesn't run if navigate returns before generating the ID (the sandboxing check), so callers with a non-null source document would need to handle that.\n\n<details><summary>Reviewed commits</summary>\n\nReviewed at 0e67ffe on 790ce89, with web-platform-tests/wpt#63659 at a4db55d, using spec-pr-review.\n</details>\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
